{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"b70b31e6-3857-4143-8318-ba7a2a21f1ec","step_index":26,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.238252282,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"head -n 25 audit/evidence/verify/F-007/10-expected-vs-actual.txt audit/evidence/verify/F-008/10-expected-vs-actual.txt audit/evidence/verify/F-007/04-mutation-check.txt audit/evidence/verify/F-008/04-mutation-check.txt"},"output":"Created At: 2026-11-23T04:56:06+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-23T04:56:06+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n==\u003e audit/evidence/verify/F-007/10-expected-vs-actual.txt \u003c==\r\n=== STEP 10: EXPECTED VS ACTUAL (TRIPLE) FOR F-007 ===\r\nFinding: F-007\r\nTitle: Missing row-level lock in sales order approval allows concurrent orders to exceed ATP stock by over 100%\r\n\r\n1. EXPECTED (source: CDI Benchmark Specification Item 6, docs/product-requirements.md REQ-027, docs/business-rules.md):\r\n   Order approval must atomically reserve available-to-promise (ATP) stock. Total active reservations for any SKU must never exceed physical on-hand stock (`sum(active reservations) \u003c= currentStock`). Under concurrent requests exceeding available stock, requests must fail with HTTP 400 Insufficient Stock.\r\n\r\n2. ACTUAL (observed with evidence):\r\n   - Commit `7c81a65d49ae7d10d3b028e13cea071e7e0fd22e` acquires row-level locks on `inventory_item` using `SELECT id, \"currentStock\" FROM \"inventory_item\" WHERE id = ${itemId} FOR UPDATE` in deterministic sorted order before evaluating ATP reservations.\r\n   - Fresh environment migrations and tests pass from zero (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/01-fresh-environment.txt).\r\n   - Original repro script: 10 iterations of 30 parallel requests now yield 0 oversold runs, with exactly 50/50 units reserved and 0 overselling (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/02-original-repro.txt).\r\n   - Test validity check: Reverting fix to 7c81a65~1 fails regression test (`AssertionError: expected 100 to be less than or equal to 50`), restoring fix passes (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/03-test-validity.txt).\r\n   - Mutation check: 3/3 mutants killed (remove FOR UPDATE, ignore reservations, inverted availability check); 0 surviving mutants (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/04-mutation-check.txt).\r\n   - Adversarial probes: 5/5 probes pass including 50 concurrent requests (exact 100 unit cap), 30 multi-line orders with shuffled item ordering (0 deadlocks), partial stock shortage atomic rollback (0 orphaned reservations), zero-stock rejection, and non-positive quantity overrides (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/05-adversarial-probes.txt).\r\n   - Sibling sweep: Completed and verified against sales dispatch and inventory modules (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/06-sibling-sweep.txt).\r\n   - Regression radius: Full test suite, CDI benchmark (18/18 assertions), SQL invariants (10/10 invariants), typecheck, and lint pass cleanly (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/07-regression-radius.txt).\r\n   - Diff review: Clean diff, zero scope creep, zero debug code (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/08-diff-review.txt).\r\n   - Standards check: ACID Consistency \u0026 Isolation, OWASP API10:2023, REQ-027 satisfied (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-007/09-standards-check.txt).\r\n\r\n3. DELTA:\r\n   None. The defect is completely eliminated. Concurrent sales order approvals serialize atomically on inventory rows, strictly preventing overselling.\r\n\r\n==\u003e audit/evidence/verify/F-008/10-expected-vs-actual.txt \u003c==\r\n=== STEP 10: EXPECTED VS ACTUAL (TRIPLE) FOR F-008 ===\r\nFinding: F-008\r\nTitle: Non-atomic `count()` based dispatch sequence generation causes unique constraint crashes on concurrent dispatches\r\n\r\n1. EXPECTED (source: docs/architecture.md, docs/product-requirements.md REQ-031):\r\n   Physical dispatch operations must be reliable, concurrent, and crash-free. Dispatch document numbers must be assigned atomically without collisions or transaction rollbacks.\r\n\r\n2. ACTUAL (observed with evidence):\r\n   - Commit `32647afc08e3ff108d0bd5e870868d13e56b2b49` replaces non-atomic `tx.dispatch.count()` with atomic row-locked UPSERT sequence generator `sequenceService.getNextDispatchNumber()` operating on `document_sequences` table.\r\n   - Fresh environment migrations and tests pass from zero (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/01-fresh-environment.txt).\r\n   - Original repro script: 10 iterations of parallel dispatches succeed with 0 failures and 0 unique constraint collisions (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/02-original-repro.txt).\r\n   - Test validity check: Reverting fix to 32647af~1 fails regression test with 9 unique constraint errors (`Unique constraint failed on dispatch_organizationId_dispatchNumber_key`), restoring fix passes (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/03-test-validity.txt).\r\n   - Mutation check: 3/3 mutants killed (no sequence increment on conflict, static dispatch suffix, truncated padding); 0 surviving mutants (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/04-mutation-check.txt).\r\n   - Adversarial probes: 4/4 probes pass including 50 concurrent dispatches (0 collisions, 50 unique numbers), multi-organization sequence isolation, year rollover segregation, and document sequence row integrity (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/05-adversarial-probes.txt).\r\n   - Sibling sweep: Identified credit note and payment receipt numbering siblings, which are tracked under CLUSTER-03 (F-013) (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/06-sibling-sweep.txt).\r\n   - Regression radius: Full test suite, CDI benchmark (18/18 assertions), SQL invariants (10/10 invariants), typecheck, and lint pass cleanly (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/07-regression-radius.txt).\r\n   - Diff review: Clean diff, zero scope creep, zero debug code (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/08-diff-review.txt).\r\n   - Standards check: ACID Concurrency, OWASP API10:2023, REQ-031 satisfied (evidence: audit/evidence/verify/F-008/09-standards-check.txt).\r\n\r\n3. DELTA:\r\n   None. The defect is completely eliminated. Concurrent dispatches allocate sequential, unique dispatch numbers without unique constraint collisions or HTTP 500 errors.\r\n\r\n==\u003e audit/evidence/verify/F-007/04-mutation-check.txt \u003c==\r\n=== STEP 4: MUTATION CHECK FOR F-007 ===\r\nTimestamp: 2026-11-23T04:43:51+05:30\r\n1. Cleaning up scratch directory and db...\r\nNOTICE:  database \"mill_ledger_mutant_f007\" does not exist, skipping\r\n2. Setting up scratch worktree at commit HEAD...\r\nPreparing worktree (detached HEAD 32647af)\r\nHEAD is now at 32647af F-008: Non-atomic `count()` based dispatch sequence generation causes unique constraint crashes on concurrent dispatches\r\nScope: all 4 workspace projects\r\n[WARN] The store at /home/snehan/.local/share/pnpm/store/v11 is not used because packages cannot be hard linked from it into this project. Using the store at /tmp/.pnpm-store/v11 instead. Set storeDir to choose the store.\r\n✓ Lockfile passes supply-chain policies (verified 4d ago)\r\nLockfile is up to date, resolution step is skipped\r\nPackages are hard linked from the content-addressable store to the virtual store.\r\n  Content-addressable store is at: /tmp/.pnpm-store/v11\r\n  Virtual store is at:             node_modules/.pnpm\r\nPackages: +876\r\n++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\r\nProgress: resolved 876, reused 876, downloaded 0, added 876, done\r\n\r\ndevDependencies:\r\n+ @playwright/test 1.65.1\r\n+ @types/node 22.20.5\r\n+ oxlint 1.94.0\r\n+ prettier 3.10.1\r\n+ typescript 5.9.3\r\n+ vitest 3.2.7\r\n\r\n==\u003e audit/evidence/verify/F-008/04-mutation-check.txt \u003c==\r\n=== STEP 4: MUTATION CHECK FOR F-008 ===\r\nTimestamp: 2026-11-23T04:44:56+05:30\r\n1. Cleaning up scratch directory and db...\r\nNOTICE:  database \"mill_led