\r\nFinding: F-007\r\nCategory: Data Integrity / Concurrency / Inventory Ledger\r\nStandards Refs: ACID Consistency \u0026 Isolation, OWASP API Security Top 10:2023 API10:2023, REQ-027\r\n\r\n1. Applicable Standards:\r\n   - ACID Consistency and Isolation:\r\n     Under PostgreSQL's default `READ COMMITTED` transaction isolation, concurrent transactions reading uncommitted state without row locks perform interleaved check-then-act operations. Row-level exclusive locking via `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` serializes concurrent transactions at the database engine level, guaranteeing serializability of ATP stock evaluations and reservation writes.\r\n   - Resource Ordering \u0026 Deadlock Freedom (Dijkstra):\r\n     Acquiring multi-row exclusive locks in deterministic sorted order (`involvedItemIds.sort()`) eliminates cyclic wait conditions in PostgreSQL's wait-for graph, mathematically guaranteeing deadlock prevention across concurrent multi-line order approvals.\r\n   - OWASP API Security Top 10:2023 API10:2023 (Unsafe Consumption of APIs / Concurrency \u0026 Race Conditions):\r\n     Concurrent API requests to resource-allocation endpoints must not result in overselling or duplicate commitment of finite assets.\r\n   - Product Requirement REQ-027 \u0026 CDI Benchmark Specification Item 6:\r\n     Mandates that total active stock reservations for any inventory item must never exceed physical on-hand stock (`sum(active reservations) \u003c= currentStock`). Under concurrent approval requests exceeding available stock, excess requests must fail with HTTP 400 Insufficient Stock.\r\n\r\n2. Evidence of Compliance:\r\n   - `server/src/modules/sales/sales.service.ts` acquires row locks on all involved inventory items using `SELECT id, \"currentStock\" FROM \"inventory_item\" WHERE id = ${itemId} FOR UPDATE` in deterministic sorted order.\r\n   - 20 concurrent approvals test in `server/src/sales-concurrency.test.ts` passes with exactly 5 approvals, 15 rejections, and total reservations \u003c= 50 units.\r\n   - 10 iterations of 30 parallel requests in `audit/scripts/verify-concurrency-approve-dispatch.ts` produced 0 oversold runs (100% pass rate).\r\n   - Adversarial Probe 1: 50 concurrent requests against 100 units reserved exactly 100 units (10 approved, 40 rejected).\r\n   - Adversarial Probe 2: 30 concurrent multi-line orders with reverse/shuffled line items produced 0 deadlocks (zero PostgreSQL 40P01 errors).\r\n   - Adversarial Probe 3: Partial stock failure triggered atomic transaction rollback with 0 orphaned reservations.\r\n   - 3 deliberate mutants killed with 0 survivors.\r\n\r\n3. Status: VERIFIED-PASS.\r\n"}}}
